70	  /// inline error, sheet never opens") — the same failure is also
71	  /// emitted as [ExportJobState.error] so the caller can read [state] for
72	  /// [Failure.message] without this method also having to hand back the
73	  /// raw `Failure` itself (the `Either<Failure, T>` shape, RNF09, is the
74	  /// repository's own contract, not every cubit method's).
